    "description": "Deprecated is a native PHP attribute. It marks a method, function or class constant as available, but soon to be removed. \n\nThe Deprecated attribute accepts an argument, that is shown to help users move to an alternative.",
    "code": "<?php\n\n#[Deprecated]\nfunction trumpet() {}\n\ntrumpet();\n//Deprecated: Function trumpet() is deprecated\n\n#[Deprecated('Use forage instead.')]\nfunction trample() {}\n\ntrample();\n//Deprecated: Function trample() is deprecated, Use forage instead.\n\n?>",
